  Fail to launch spot job due to wheels not found
Hi Sky team,

I try to launch a spot job on a new controller with the latest sky from `git pull` The job keeps failing, and the log error is

```
(warmup pid=534) I 09-01 01:04:42 recovery_strategy.py:144] Failed to launch the spot cluster with error: Could not find built SkyPilot wheels 'skypilot-1.0.0.dev0-*.whl' under PosixPath('/home/.../.sky/sky_wheels')
(warmup pid=534) I 09-01 01:04:42 recovery_strategy.py:175] Retrying to launch the spot cluster in 95.6 seconds.
(warmup pid=534) I 09-01 01:06:17 cloud_vm_ray_backend.py:2666] Creating a new cluster: "warmup-1" [1x GCP(n2d-standard-4[Spot])].
(warmup pid=534) I 09-01 01:06:17 cloud_vm_ray_backend.py:2666] Tip: to reuse an existing cluster, specify --cluster (-c). Run `sky status` to see existing clusters.
(warmup pid=534) No existing clusters.
(warmup pid=534)
(warmup pid=534) I 09-01 01:06:19 recovery_strategy.py:144] Failed to launch the spot cluster with error: Could not find built SkyPilot wheels 'skypilot-1.0.0.dev0-*.whl' under PosixPath('/home/.../.sky/sky_wheels')
(warmup pid=534) E 09-01 01:06:19 controller.py:131] Resources unavailable: Failed to launch the spot cluster after 3 retries.
(warmup pid=534) I 09-01 01:06:19 spot_state.py:186] Job failed due to failing to find available resources after retries.
``` 

And I go to `~/.sky/sky_wheels/`, the whl file exists, but located in a sub-dir named by its hash.
```
~$ tree ~/.sky/sky_wheels/
/home/qzeng_salk_edu/.sky/sky_wheels/
├── 6567324f0436356cf90d23feaebc2e10
│   └── skypilot-1.0.0.dev0-py3-none-any.whl
├── current_sky_wheel_hash
```

If I copy the `skypilot-1.0.0.dev0-py3-none-any.whl` file to `~/.sky/sky_wheels/`, the spot job succeed.

In my older controllers, the whl file do exist in `~/.sky/sky_wheels/` without the sub-dir.
  </issue>
  
